---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

// Fully static: no session, no cookies, nothing dynamic. Header reads only
// `Astro.url.pathname`, so this serves as a file. That matters because a third
// party (Intervals' OAuth registration review) fetches this page.
export const prerender = true;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy — Stride Lab"
  description="What Stride Lab stores, who it is shared with, and how to get it deleted."
  heading="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
>
  <p>
    Stride Lab is a running training plan that adjusts tomorrow's session from
    what you logged today. This page says exactly what we store, who else sees
    it, and how to make us delete it. Effective 27 September 2026.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    What we store
  </h2>

  <h3 class="font-semibold text-cloud">Account</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
    <li>Your email address, and whether it has been verified.</li>
    <li>
      If you sign in with Google, the Google account identifier Google returns
      to us. If you use a password, a hash of it — never the password itself.
    </li>
    <li>Session cookies and the date your account was created.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="font-semibold text-cloud">Training</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
    <li>Your plan, the sessions on it, and the feedback you leave on a session.</li>
    <li>
      Run logs you enter: date, distance, duration, pace, and how the entry was
      made.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you record a route, the GPS trace and its samples. Without a recorded
      route, we store no location data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="font-semibold text-cloud">Intervals.icu connection</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
    <li>
      Your Intervals athlete ID, display name, the scopes you granted, and when
      we last synced.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your Intervals API key or access token, encrypted at rest. It is never
      displayed in the app and never sent to a browser.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    Who else sees your data
  </h2>

  <p>
    We do not sell your data, and we run no analytics, advertising, or
    third-party tracking of any kind. Four services see some of it, and only
    these four:
  </p>

  <h3 class="font-semibold text-cloud">Ollama Cloud — for AI coaching</h3>
  <p>
    To write coaching feedback and adjust your next session, we send a limited
    snapshot of your training to a language model served by
    <a
      class="underline decoration-lime/50 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-lime"
      href="https://ollama.com/privacy">Ollama Cloud</a>. That snapshot can
    include average, maximum and resting heart rate, your lactate threshold and
    athlete maximum, cadence, step rate, distance, duration, pace, and the
    feedback you left on a session. It does not include your email address, your
    name, or any account identifier. If you would rather we did not send this,
    tell us and we will turn the AI features off for your account.
  </p>

  <h3 class="font-semibold text-cloud">Intervals.icu</h3>
  <p>
    Only if you connect. We exchange authorisation tokens with them to import
    your activities and to write planned runs to your calendar.
  </p>

  <h3 class="font-semibold text-cloud">Resend</h3>
  <p>
    Only if you use a magic link. They deliver the sign-in email and see your
    address for that delivery.
  </p>

  <h3 class="font-semibold text-cloud">Google</h3>
  <p>Only if you choose Google sign-in.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    Where it lives
  </h2>
  <p>
    In a single SQLite database on our own server. Not in a third-party
    database, and not in a cloud data warehouse.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    How long we keep it
  </h2>
  <p>
    Until you ask us to delete it. We keep training history so your plan and
    progress still work, which means we cannot delete your account while also
    keeping your data. One request does both.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    Your choices
  </h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
    <li>Disconnect Intervals.icu at any time in Settings.</li>
    <li>Edit or delete individual run logs and session feedback yourself.</li>
    <li>
      Ask us to stop using the AI features, which stops all data reaching Ollama
      Cloud.
    </li>
    <li>
      Ask us to export or delete your account and everything in it. We will
      confirm when it is done.
    </li>
    <li>Withdraw consent at any time, and stop using the service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    Security
  </h2>
  <p>
    Intervals credentials are encrypted before they are written. Passwords are
    stored only as hashes. Signing out revokes the session. We do not consider
    any of this a substitute for a strong password.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    Children
  </h2>
  <p>
    Stride Lab is not for anyone under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from
    children.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    Changes
  </h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes we will update the date at the top. Material changes
    will be announced in the app before they take effect.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-cloud uppercase">
    Contact
  </h2>
  <p>
    Questions, exports, or deletion requests:
    <a
      class="underline decoration-lime/50 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-lime"
      href="mailto:crispal94@gmail.com">crispal94@gmail.com</a
    >.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
